roy hashimoto has presented a scenario that seems to me to border on
unfair. i wouldn't feel that way if i could say with certainty that
there always exists a path from stairwell to stairwell that doesn't
encounter a locked door. nh3.0f3 doesn't lack shop noises.
{{{shop location spoiler ahead but very minor so read it ...}}}


shops are located extremely on the left or right side of a floor.
this fact, together with the noise that shopkeepers make let's you
know fairly certainly when you've reached a shop. there can only be
one shop on a floor and there is only one natural path (corridor)
leading up to it. you undoubtably know that kicking down someone's
door is not to be done lightly, so if you found the door locked you
could have come back to it when you could peaceably open it with
perhaps a key, lock pick, or a magic spell. then again, you could
have dug into the shop or have had a monster do the dirty work.
teleporting in at that point of the game is unlikely.

good job roy! i hope your observation makes nh3 a better game ...

